# Sentinel EC (always on)

Help submit **Sentinel Ultra** tasks that pass Snorkel evals and get **Accept**.

## User drops zips in tasks/inbox/

When they say they added a zip, run `./scripts/ingest-task.sh <filename>` first.

## Before upload

1. `./scripts/sync-problem-statement.sh tasks/active/<name>`
2. `./scripts/preflight.sh tasks/active/<name>` — clean, including oracle 1.0 / NOP 0.0
3. `./scripts/zip-task.sh tasks/active/<name>`

## Hard rules

- Never edit tracked files in `environment/repo/`
- **11–20** fail-to-pass; pass-to-pass unchanged at base
- instruction ↔ tests coverage + faithfulness
- PR scope: expand OK, reduce/replace → Not Fixable
- `tests.patch` must not create files at paths an agent may also create
- Revision budget is 2: eval runs are free, reviewer round-trips are not
  (`docs/REVISION-BUDGET.md`)
- A rule is decided in one file (see "Where a rule lives" in `AGENTS.md`); when a doc and a
  check disagree, the check wins — edit the rule at its source, never only at a copy

## Workflow

When the user adds a zip or says "I added `<name>.zip`", read `docs/SENTINEL-PROMPTS.md`
and run Steps 0 → 1 → 2 → 3 → 4 automatically unless they ask to stop or skip a step.
Use the "If this happens…" branches only when that situation applies.

## Learnings log (mandatory)

- **Start:** Read `docs/EC-LEARNINGS.md` (Standing rules + last 5 entries) and `docs/PLATFORM-TRIAGE.md` before any task work.
- **End:** Append a session log entry to `docs/EC-LEARNINGS.md` when work stops — no user prompt needed.
- **Skip:** If criteria in `docs/SKIP-GUIDE.md` match, recommend skip with copy-paste reason — do not keep revising.
- Promote repeated mistakes to Standing rules in that file.
